{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382349-ratkin-and-wood-mouses","id":1382349,"title":"Ratkin and Wood Mouses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-18T10:53:10-07:00","id":1382349,"title":"Ratkin and Wood Mouses","content":"Hi.<br /> <br /> I have a simple question:<br /> <br /> Can Roden Ratkin come from wood mouses or they necessarily have to come from the regular city-sewer rat? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:09:06-07:00","id":1382363,"title":"","content":"If I recall they could come from any kind of genus of Rattus (Black rat, Kerala rat, Tanezumi rat, etc), not only the Brown Rat (aka Sewer rat), but they can't come from mice, gerbils or anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:01:58-07:00","id":1382757,"title":"","content":"The Ratkin books mentions the Spiny Rat, which is an Echimyidae native to Central and South America. The book implies that species/family (sorry, not a biologist) is accepted, but there's no clarity about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 04-20-2020, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:18:20-07:00","id":1382772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382349-ratkin-and-wood-mouses?p=1382757#post1382757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ratkin books mentions the Spiny Rat, which is an Echimyidae native to Central and South America. The book implies that species/family (sorry, not a biologist) is accepted, but there's no clarity about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ratkin book also incorrectly reported that kangaroo rats were marsupials. In this case, the spiny rat is pretty far off from being a rat-rat, because it's actually more like a guinea pig or chinchilla, and in the same boat of life as the coypu. So unless you also allow for werenutrias, it's probably a no-go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T14:38:16-07:00","id":1382826,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've been toying with the Idea that in Prehistory the Ratkin were spread among many types of Rats and mice in prehistory, but with the rise of cities they pretty much entirely shifted to Rattus Rattus. Maybe some of their Nightmare Genetic Memory of being Slain by Garou and the like in Prehistory were amplified by them having to find different Animal Kinfolk eventually settling on Rattus Rattus in modern times.<br /> <br /> Another thing that seems to not make sense is domesticated animals seem to loose the spark that permits changebreed souls, hence the loss of Apis and Grondr kinfolk. But we have a Freak Aspect of Ratkin that are from the inbred domesticated white lab rats. I don't know maybe their Wyld Spark gives them a unique exception to the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T19:04:35-07:00","id":1383067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382349-ratkin-and-wood-mouses?p=1382826#post1382826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that seems to not make sense is domesticated animals seem to loose the spark that permits changebreed souls, hence the loss of Apis and Grondr kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand the logic, I don't think that's a thing that applies to the entire species. Dogs, after all, are the oldest domesticated animal and they derive from wolves. So imply having derived domesticated animals doesn't do anything. And wild aurochs and boars, like wolves, still existed long after some of their members became domesticated. While the aurochs eventually went extinct in the 17th century, we still have wild boars around. So there were plenty of wild animals that could have been kinfolk for thousands of years after their related Changing Breed died.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T19:12:36-07:00","id":1383069,"title":"","content":"Well the Grondr lost their kin while they were being genocided, some of the warcrimes during the War of Rage was the Werewolves convinced the corrupt, leeches, of the first cities to enslave the Grondr human kin and domesticate their animal kin.<br /> <br /> But Grondr apparently were confined to Eurasia, and they didn't spread to the New World.<br /> <br /> But Werewolves can't breed with dogs and get a chance of Garou as a result, or even viable kinfolk whelped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T01:53:04-07:00","id":1383109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1382349-ratkin-and-wood-mouses?p=1383069#post1383069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Grondr lost their kin while they were being genocided, some of the warcrimes during the War of Rage was the Werewolves convinced the corrupt, leeches, of the first cities to enslave the Grondr human kin and domesticate their animal kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't know that was the story in the sourcebooks. Thanks for sharing it.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of things written about the War of Rage, that doesn't make sense to me. The range of wild boar, and thus the area where Grondr could have existed, was a pretty big area. and a lot of that territory was simply not areas where cities, civilization, and mass slavery existed in the likely time period of the War of Rage. So the idea that Grondr human kinfolk living in modern day Mongolia, Kazakhstan, Sweden, and many other places could have been enslaved by early civilizations in the Fertile Crescent isn't realistic. And as for animal kinfolk, pigs were only domesticated independently twice around 10.000 years ago in Mesopotamia and China. All strains of pigs descend from those. And once you begin to domesticate the animal, there is almost no incentive to reintroduce wild stock into your population - it would ruin those traits you are selecting for. So the idea that all the Grondr animal kinfolk worldwide were domesticated thousands of years after domestic pigs existed, doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> I understand that the sourcebooks were written by people that either didn't study the history of animal domestication, or simply didn't care. And if you don't particularly care either, that's fine too. But for me, that's not a convincing backstory. But as I said, LOTS of things that are the &quot;official&quot; story of the War of Rage doesn't make sense to me, and I ignore it and have my own explanations for my chronicles (not that it ever comes up in game as a practical exercise).<br /> <br /> I actually agree with you that domesticated stock should lose the Changing Breed &quot;gene&quot; (or spark as you call it). I just don't think that applies to why any of the Breeds have gone extinct.<br /> <br /> I think there's a much simpler explanation. All the Changing Breeds struggled for territory for their kinfolk. This lead to a lot of conflicts as the world filled up to whatever the carrying capacity was at that time. Everyone was fighting each other. That works for hunter-gatherers and pastoralists too, not just urban civilizations. And it isn't a surprise that the Changing Breeds that survived were based on predator species, while the Breeds that became extinct were based on prey species. There are exceptions to that general rule, but it's obvious why they are exceptions. Ravens can fly away, and Rats are small burrowers that breed like crazy for example. Not a surprise they survived. The big prey animals that couldn't get away went away. That wasn't intentional, it just happened. Just like how many species became extinct.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, do you know there's been concerted efforts since the 1920s to try to bring back the wild aurochs? It's a rather fascinating story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:58:20-07:00","id":1389120,"title":"","content":"Well I think that for certain, most of the kinfolk carrying the Grondr and Apis blood were simply killed. The books do say that some of the <b>last</b> of the kinfolk were enslaved or domesticated, with others degenerating into Skull Pigs. In the case of the Grondr, CB20 claims they bred with a now-extinct (imaginary) boar species, and that some of their homid kinfolk lines may still exist in diluted form.<br /> <br /> None of the books actually said that the extinction of the aurochs in the 2nd millennium was connected to the Apis extinction in the War of Rage... only that it guarantees they can't possibly be revived.<br /> <br /> Sandchigger, I was thinking exactly the same thing about the Ratkin. I looked at the range of the genus Rattus and wondered how Ratkin were supposed to do their jobs in Africa and Europe with no kinfolk. So I figured they used to breed with African and Middle-East <i>Arvicanthis</i> as well. Given that they can breed with Sumatran giant rats, it doesn't seem that far-fetched -- then again, I think their phenomenal Wyld taint is responsible for their ability to breed with unrelated rodents like African giant pouched rats, and to breed true with lab rats, as well as their Freak Aspects.<br /> <br /> I also imagine them originally breeding with Australian native rats, though, and then wonder what happened to all those Koori Ratkin and their Bards...<br /> <br /> Seriously guys, what did happen to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}